x760 text "Views and edits"
x761 puts x759 x760
x762 call close x761 
x763 call open x762 2
x764 write x763 2
x765 text "A model never sees a whole file. It asks for a view of one function: the function with a handle line on top (e0) and, when the whole program matters, a program handle (g0) with one signature line per function. A reply is the handle line followed by edits, one per line: `id op ...` replaces the instruction id or inserts it before ret; `id op ... @ other` inserts after other; `-id` deletes; `ret x` changes the result. Under g0, a whole `fn ... end` block adds or replaces a function and `-fn name` removes one. The edit is applied only if it parses, type-checks, validates, and was written against the current revision; otherwise it is rejected and the handle stays valid."
